Implement user story AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Story Description
[GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Acceptance Criteria
- 


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): This is where the content object is COMPUTED and provided to all 236+ useContent consumers. Currently it uses useMemo with a static defaultContent dependency, producing an immutable context value that never updates after initial render. For live preview to work, this provider must be able to receive and propagate content updates from Contentstack's live preview SDK — and since useContent reads exclusively from this context, fixing it here automatically benefits every consumer.
  - **Minimal fix:** Replace the useMemo block (lines 56-61) with useState to make content mutable, then add a useEffect that initializes Contentstack live preview (import from '@contentstack/live-preview-utils') and calls the state setter on each edit callback. The provider already receives defaultContent as a prop — use it as the initial state. The useContent hook and all 236+ consumers read from this context via getContentByKey, so they receive updates automatically with no other changes. No existing live-preview helper exists in this repo (confirmed by ripgrep: live_preview, livePreview, ContentstackLivePreview all NOT FOUND), so the @contentstack/live-preview-utils SDK must be introduced here.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- With the application running and a page rendered from CMS content, when a CMS editor modifies a content field in Contentstack, the tester observes the rendered page update to display the new value without any manual browser refresh or republish.
- When a CMS content edit is reflected in the running application, the tester observes the update appears in place: the browser does not perform a full page reload, and the current page, scroll position, and in-app state are preserved.
- After a CMS editor modifies content used by multiple different pages and components, the tester observes that every rendered location displaying that content shows the updated value, across a representative sample of the application's content-driven screens.
- On initial load of the application, the tester observes that pages render the currently published CMS content correctly, with no missing, stale, or broken content compared to before live preview was introduced.
- When a CMS editor makes a second, subsequent content change after a first change has already been reflected, the tester observes the rendered page update again to show the latest value, confirming updates continue to arrive over time rather than only once.

## Tests are NOT your job this turn
A dedicated test-writer agent runs immediately after your fix commits and owns the bug-reproducing test. Do NOT write, edit, or create any test file (*.test.*, *.spec.*, __tests__/). Write ONLY the fix. Adding a test here wastes your turn budget and has caused repeated failures.

